Uma Bellows website  (https://umabellows.com)

Static HTML/CSS site served by GitHub Pages from the main branch.
Merging into main publishes the site within a minute or two.

LAYOUT
  index.html, <section>/index.html   one HTML file per page
  assets/css/site.css                all styles
  assets/js/site.js                  all scripts (no libraries)
  assets/img/                        images
  sitemap.xml, robots.txt, CNAME     search engines and the custom domain
  _partials/                         shared head, header, footer, logo strip
  tools/check_site.py                site checks (not published)
  tools/sync_partials.py             stamps _partials/ into every page
  tools/optimize_images.py           makes new photos web-sized (needs Pillow)

PREVIEW LOCALLY
  From the repository root:
    python -m http.server 8000
  then open http://localhost:8000/ (site paths start with "/", so open
  the files through the server, not by double-clicking them).

CHECK BEFORE COMMITTING
    python tools/check_site.py            all checks; exits non-zero on a problem
    python tools/check_site.py --weights  also lists image weight per page
  The same check runs automatically on every pull request.
  It verifies links, images and #anchors, that sitemap.xml lists every
  indexable page, that indexable pages have no draft text ([TBD], TODO),
  that every <img> has width and height and no image is over 1 MB, and
  that every page's shared parts match _partials/.

SHARED PAGE PARTS (_partials/, not published)
  head.html             icons, stylesheet, Content-Security-Policy, referrer policy
  header.html           logo, main menu, mobile menu
  footer.html           footer columns, address, copyright line
  clients-marquee.html  the client-logo strip (Home and About)
  Every page carries copies of these between markers such as
    <!-- partial:header --> ... <!-- /partial:header -->
  Never edit between the markers in a page. Edit the file in _partials/, then:
    python tools/sync_partials.py           stamps it into every page
    python tools/sync_partials.py --check   reports pages that are out of date
  The script also highlights the current section in the menu and writes the
  current year into the footer. In January, run it once to update the year
  (the site check fails until you do).

EDITING NOTES
  * New page: copy an existing page so it has the head, header and footer
    markers, then run tools/sync_partials.py.
  * A new indexable page must be added to sitemap.xml. Pages that are not
    ready get <meta name="robots" content="noindex"> and stay out of it.
  * The Content-Security-Policy (in _partials/head.html) only allows scripts,
    styles and images from this site, and form posts to FormSubmit. A new
    third-party script, font, embed or form service must be added to it, or
    browsers will block it.

ADDING A PHOTO
  1. Save it under assets/img/ (PNG or JPEG, as large as you have).
  2. Run, with the layout it will appear in:
       python tools/optimize_images.py --layout tile assets/img/catalog/ej/ej-15.png
     Layouts: tile (photo grids), card (product cards), hero (homepage
     slider), process (captioned photo strip), half (half-width column),
     full (full width). This writes ej-15.webp (up to 1600 px) and
     ej-15-640.webp, moves the original to _archive/originals/ (kept on this
     computer only, not published), and prints a complete <img> tag.
  3. Paste the tag into the page and write the alt text. Images in the
     first screen of a page drop loading="lazy"; full-size links point at
     the large .webp.
  4. Run python tools/check_site.py.
  Homepage slider: only the first slide has a real src. The others use
  data-src / data-srcset (with the tiny placeholder src), and site.js loads
  them when they are shown.

QUOTE FORM (contact/index.html)
  Submissions go through FormSubmit (formsubmit.co) to contact@umabellows.com.
  * The very first submission triggers a one-time activation email from
    FormSubmit to contact@umabellows.com. Someone with access to that inbox
    must click the link; until then, submissions are not delivered.
  * The activation email also gives a random-string address. Replacing the
    email in the form's action URL with it keeps the address out of the page.
  * The Privacy Policy names FormSubmit; keep it accurate if this changes.

PUSHING
  Some connections drop pushes larger than about 3 MB. Commit large image
  changes in several smaller commits and push them one at a time.
